  "reproduction_readme": "Windows Python 3.14.3; no container or external runtime services. Create a venv, install verification/acceptance-r1/runtime-requirements.txt, and pip install --no-deps -e . from the exact frozen product commit. Do not install the old baseline editable URL from raw pip freeze. Put the frozen root and verification/acceptance-r1 on PYTHONPATH; confirm pycose.__file__ is the frozen product path.\n\nRun python -B -m pytest -q -o addopts= -p no:cacheprovider --tb=short verification/acceptance-r1/test_cose_contract.py verification/acceptance-r1/test_cose_label_values.py. Expected frozen behavior: 26 pass and 3 fail. The three failures have one cause: _label_identity translates text KID and integer 4 through the same registered-attribute alias. A Critical integer 4 can be accepted without actual integer label 4, and understanding integer 4 can wrongly satisfy a different text critical label. Conversely valid distinct noncritical labels are rejected as duplicates. The inputs are hand-spliced raw CBOR and signed by freshly generated Ed25519 keys. This is a header-contract bypass, not a forged-signature demonstration.\n\npython -B verification/acceptance-r1/critical-observation-r2.py prints the two actual accepted messages with signature_valid=true; cose-demo.py shows noncanonical-byte verification, detached payload and external AAD, duplicate rejection and trailing-data rejection. The older critical-observation.stdout.log is invalid helper output: json.dumps failed on bytes after successful verification and an overly broad catch mislabeled the accepted decode as REJECTED. observation-helper-review.json explains the retained error; only the corrected r2 observation is used in Feedback/scoring.\n\npython -B -m pytest -q -o addopts= -p no:cacheprovider tests reproduces 1659 pass and 3 existing skips. The 25 strict model tests are part of that suite, not additive. Original decode remains compatible. Exact commands, logs, import locations and before/after source hashes are retained. The separately authored console demonstration is a verification helper, not a model-authored interface. The first recording attempt failed to find its window and generated no video; the delivered second attempt continuously captures all successes and the three contract failures.",
  "no_model_source_edits": true,
